course: dictionary
lesson: 785
title: Old words in stories
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bedchamber is an old, formal word for a bedroom, especially a grand bedroom in a palace or a big house. You will meet it in old stories, fairy tales and history books about kings and queens.
explain: Context helps you spot its meaning. «The bedroom is half bedchamber and half loft, half full of Badger's winter stores: apples, turnips, potatoes, nuts and jars of honey.» The word bedroom is right there, so bedchamber must mean a bedroom too. Try the swap: "half bedroom and half loft" still makes sense.
explain: Old words give a story a grand, old-fashioned feel. Bedchamber sounds more special than bedroom, so writers choose it to make a room seem royal or long ago. When you read it, picture a palace, not a tiny bedroom with a poster on the wall.
fact: A bedchamber is an old, formal word for a bedroom.
fact: «Bedchamber» is often used for a bedroom in a palace or a grand house.
fact: You will find «bedchamber» in fairy tales, the Bible and history books about kings and queens.
fact: «Lady of the Bedchamber» is a title for a queen's helper.
fact: To check a new word, swap in a simpler word like "bedroom" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: What is a bedchamber? | A garden shed for tools | *A bedroom, often a grand one | A kitchen with a big stove
exercise: In «The bedroom is half bedchamber and half loft», which word is the clue to its meaning? | Honey | *Bedroom | Loft | Turnips
exercise: Which kind of book would most likely use the word bedchamber to describe a room? | A football report | *A story about a king and queen | A recipe for apple cake | A weather forecast
test: What is «Lady of the Bedchamber»? | A cook in a farmhouse | A kind of bread | A type of small boat | *A title for a queen's helper
test: Where would a writer most likely use the word bedchamber? | In a shopping list | In a text message about homework | *In a palace in an old fairy tale | In a science experiment
exam: Why would a writer choose «bedchamber» instead of bedroom in a story about a king? | To say the room has only a bed in it | *To give a grand, old-fashioned feeling | Because bedroom is spelled wrong | To show the room is dirty
